   *   *   *   *   *
.SS Troubleshooting
\f[B]\(lqauthorization denied\(rq when opening the database\f[R] → Full
Disk Access is not granted to the correct Python binary.
Follow step 1 above \(em you need the Mach\-O binary named
\f[CR]Python\f[R], not a symlink or script in \f[CR]bin/\f[R].
Restart your Mac after making changes.
.PP
\f[B]Scheduled scan finds 0 files but terminal scan works\f[R] → Same
cause \(em FDA is missing.
The scan runs but can\(cqt read the directory.
.PP
\f[B]Python binary is grayed out in the FDA file picker\f[R] → You\(cqre
looking at \f[CR]bin/python3.XX\f[R] which is a script, not the real
binary.
Use the \f[CR]file\f[R] command to locate the Mach\-O executable \(em
it\(cqs named \f[CR]Python\f[R] (no extension) one level up from
\f[CR]bin/\f[R] in the framework directory.
.PP
\f[B]Log shows errors but \f[CB]rotbyte\f[B] works fine from the
terminal\f[R] → Your terminal has FDA (which child processes inherit),
but the launchd Python process does not.
Grant FDA to Python directly and restart.
.PP
\f[B]Plist points to a personal script instead of Homebrew\f[R] → Check
\f[CR]which rotbyte\f[R].
If it resolves to \f[CR]\(ti/.bin/rotbyte\f[R] or similar instead of
\f[CR]/opt/homebrew/bin/rotbyte\f[R], the wrong version is generating
the plist.
Remove the personal copy or use the full Homebrew path with
\f[CR]\-\-track\f[R].
.PP
\f[B]\f[CB]\-\-status\f[B] shows \f[CB]BROKEN ✗\f[B] for a schedule\f[R]
→ The plist\(cqs interpreter/script path no longer exists (usually after
a Homebrew upgrade).
Run \f[CR]rotbyte \-\-repair\f[R] to re\-point every schedule at the
current path and reload it.
.PP
\f[B]\f[CB]\-\-status\f[B] shows \(lqno scheduled scans found\(rq\f[R] →
The plist may be malformed.
Verify with:
.IP
.EX
python3 \-c \(dqimport plistlib; plistlib.load(open(\(aq$HOME/Library/LaunchAgents/com.rotbyte.quick.HASH.plist\(aq, \(aqrb\(aq))\(dq
.EE
.PP
If this fails, update to v1.1.0+ and re\-run \f[CR]\-\-track\f[R] to
regenerate.
.PP
\f[B]\f[CB]\-\-full\-at\f[B] consumes the directory path as a time
argument\f[R] → \f[CR]\-\-full\-at\f[R] accepts multiple values and is
greedy.
Put the path before it:
.IP
.EX
rotbyte \-\-track \(ti/Desktop \-\-full\-at 2h
.EE
.PP
\f[B]FDA changes don\(cqt take effect\f[R] → Restart your Mac.
Logging out and back in is not enough for launchd agents.
